Originally, Everyman was a 5/6 monster for the cost of 8G released in '''Beta 4.2'''. '''Beta 4.5''' nerfed it with -1 HP, but '''Beta 7.1''' buffed it with -1 Cost, leaving it at 5/5 for 7G.

'''Beta 19.0''' gave it its first change in its effect. Before, it just had the ability of being unable to take damage during your turn. Now, it gained a Magic effect with it. A Magic effect that gives +2/+2 to a random ally [http://undercards.wikia.com/wiki/Category:Amalgamate Amalgamate]. '''Beta 30.0''' not only nerfed the effect to only give +1/+1, Everyman itself also gained -1 in all its stats.

'''Beta 41.1''' gave it +1 ATK and reworked its Magic. Now, it'll let you add an exact copy of an ally Amalgamate to your hand, making it a monster (but Tribe limited) version of [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Cloning Cloning]. '''Beta 42.0''' made it unable to target another Everyman.
